# Content-addressed vault blobs: never transform them.
#
# Each file's NAME is the SHA-256 of its CONTENT, so any end-of-line conversion
# silently invalidates the dataset — the seeder would copy bytes into the vault
# that no longer hash to the name it looked them up by. Git cannot infer this:
# it classifies by content, and STEP and SVG payloads are plain ASCII, so with
# core.autocrlf=true it would happily rewrite them on checkout and hand Windows
# and Linux users different datasets.
freecad-demo/files/** binary

# The table dumps are JSON and stay LF everywhere, so a re-bake compares clean.
freecad-demo/**/*.json text eol=lf
freecad-demo/README.md text eol=lf

# The robot arm's manifest and its per-model node lists, for the same reason and
# one more: this dataset ships as a Docker image built from a checkout, so a
# maintainer building on Windows has to produce the same bytes as CI does on
# Linux. Without this the node lists check out CRLF here and LF there, and
# `robot-arm/manifest.json` had already drifted that way on disk.
robot-arm/**/*.json text eol=lf
robot-arm/README.md text eol=lf
